{"v":15,"id":"e12","kid":"emma","title":"Thanksgiving in North America","zh":"北美的感恩节","level":"A2+","genre":"节日文化 · 北美","src":"facts","sum":"加拿大和美国都过感恩节，但日期不同。人们团聚吃火鸡和南瓜派、说出感恩的事、看游行，也去食物银行做志愿者。","words":282,"paras":[{"t":"Thanksgiving is one of the biggest holidays in the United States and Canada. It is a time for families and friends to get together, share a big meal and give thanks for the good things in their lives.","w":[[0,12,"Thanksgiving",-1],[13,15,"is",-1],[16,19,"one",-1],[20,22,"of",-1],[23,26,"the",-1],[27,34,"biggest",-1],[35,43,"holidays",-1],[44,46,"in",-1],[47,50,"the",1],[51,57,"United",1],[58,64,"States",1],[65,68,"and",-1],[69,75,"canada",-1],[77,79,"it",-1],[80,82,"is",-1],[83,84,"a",-1],[85,89,"time",-1],[90,93,"for",-1],[94,102,"families",-1],[103,106,"and",-1],[107,114,"friends",-1],[115,117,"to",-1],[118,121,"get",0],[122,130,"together",0],[132,137,"share",-1],[138,139,"a",-1],[140,143,"big",-1],[144,148,"meal",-1],[149,152,"and",-1],[153,157,"give",2],[158,164,"thanks",2],[165,168,"for",-1],[169,172,"the",-1],[173,177,"good",-1],[178,184,"things",-1],[185,187,"in",-1],[188,193,"their",-1],[194,199,"lives",-1]]},{"t":"The two countries celebrate on different days. In Canada, Thanksgiving is on the second Monday of October. In the United States, it is on the fourth Thursday of November. Many Americans get both Thursday and Friday off, so they have a four-day weekend. Because so many people travel home, it is one of the busiest times of the year at airports and on highways.","w":[[0,3,"the",-1],[4,7,"two",-1],[8,17,"countries",-1],[18,27,"celebrate",-1],[28,30,"on",-1],[31,40,"different",-1],[41,45,"days",-1],[47,49,"in",-1],[50,56,"canada",-1],[58,70,"Thanksgiving",-1],[71,73,"is",-1],[74,76,"on",-1],[77,80,"the",-1],[81,87,"second",-1],[88,94,"monday",-1],[95,97,"of",-1],[98,105,"october",-1],[107,109,"in",-1],[110,113,"the",1],[114,120,"United",1],[121,127,"States",1],[129,131,"it",-1],[132,134,"is",-1],[135,137,"on",-1],[138,141,"the",-1],[